"🦉 tea first

📜 education.pedigree
   ├─ what = the record of what each role was taught: pursuits, courses, greats, claims
   ├─ usage
   │  ├─ rhx education.pedigree get [--for <role>]
   │  └─ rhx education.pedigree set [--from <pursuit route>]
   ├─ inputs
   │  ├─ --for (get) one role; default every role this repo holds
   │  └─ --from (set) the pursuit to stamp; default the bound one
   ├─ examples
   │  ├─ rhx education.pedigree get --for mechanic
   │  └─ rhx education.pedigree set   # from 4.graduate of a pursuit
   └─ exit = 0 done · 1 malfunction · 2 refused, with its fix"
`;

exports[`education faces given: [case1] a repo with a native mechanic, on a feature branch when: [t0] each face is asked for help then: each renders as the snapshot shows: pursuit --help 1`] = `
"🦉 tea first

📜 education.pursuit
   ├─ what = send a role on a pursuit: courses from the greats, then graduation
   ├─ usage
   │  └─ rhx education.pursuit init --for <role> --slug <slug> [--course <slug>…]
   ├─ inputs
   │  ├─ --for (required) the role to educate: own, linked, or native to this repo
   │  ├─ --slug the pursuit name, kebab; defaults to the course when one --course is named
   │  └─ --course a course to seed the plot, in order; repeatable
   ├─ examples
   │  ├─ rhx education.pursuit init --for mechanic --course idempotency
   │  └─ rhx education.pursuit init --for mechanic --slug reliable-writes --course idempotency --course retries
   ├─ guard verb = judge --criterion plot-valid|courses-exited|pedigree-stamped|boot-within-budget --route $route
   └─ exit = 0 done · 1 malfunction · 2 refused, with its fix"
`;

